1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,590
Every tenant of an Orchard Core application shares the files of the application's wwwroot folder.

2
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:13,156
The Static File Provider feature gives each tenant its own wwwroot folder, served

3
00:00:13,156 --> 00:00:15,075
at the tenant's address.

4
00:00:15,075 --> 00:00:19,170
In this video, we enable it, add files, and read its code.

5
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:28,749
The static files of the application live in its wwwroot folder, and every

6
00:00:28,749 --> 00:00:30,703
tenant is served from it.

7
00:00:30,703 --> 00:00:34,674
A file there belongs to the application, not to a tenant.

8
00:00:34,674 --> 00:00:39,780
A robots.txt or a favicon that differs between tenants needs another place.

9
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:44,801
The Static File Provider feature gives each tenant that enables it a file

10
00:00:44,801 --> 00:00:46,206
provider of its own.

11
00:00:46,206 --> 00:00:50,423
Its files are served under the tenant's domain and URL prefix, even when

12
00:00:50,423 --> 00:00:53,180
another tenant has files with the same names.

13
00:00:57,429 --> 00:00:59,779
Let's enable the feature on a tenant.

14
00:00:59,779 --> 00:01:02,893
On the Default tenant, open Multi-Tenancy, Tenants.

15
00:01:02,893 --> 00:01:08,249
Each running tenant besides Default has a Features button, so let's select the one of Maple.

16
00:01:08,815 --> 00:01:11,933
The page lists the features of the Maple tenant.

17
00:01:11,933 --> 00:01:16,900
Searching for static finds Static File Provider, in the Infrastructure category.

18
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,175
It provides a way to serve independent static files for each tenant.

19
00:01:21,685 --> 00:01:25,947
Select Enable, and a message confirms that the feature was enabled.

20
00:01:25,947 --> 00:01:29,684
A tenant can also enable it itself, under Tools, Features:

21
00:01:29,684 --> 00:01:32,895
the feature is not limited to the Default tenant.

22
00:01:34,495 --> 00:01:38,549
A recipe enables it with the feature step, which lists the features to

23
00:01:38,549 --> 00:01:40,043
enable and to disable.

24
00:01:40,043 --> 00:01:43,457
Add it to the recipe that sets up a tenant, and the tenant

25
00:01:43,457 --> 00:01:45,485
starts with the feature enabled.

26
00:01:49,685 --> 00:01:55,617
Each tenant's files go in the wwwroot folder of its site folder, under App_Data, Sites.

27
00:01:55,617 --> 00:02:00,783
The folder is named after the tenant, here Maple, not after its URL prefix.

28
00:02:00,783 --> 00:02:03,845
The feature creates it when it is missing.

29
00:02:04,595 --> 00:02:08,396
You copy the files to the server yourself, since the feature has no

30
00:02:08,396 --> 00:02:09,855
screen to upload them.

31
00:02:09,855 --> 00:02:14,125
A file in a subfolder is served at the same path under the tenant's address.

32
00:02:18,376 --> 00:02:24,759
Maple's URL prefix is bakery, so its robots.txt is served at /bakery/robots.txt.

33
00:02:24,759 --> 00:02:29,436
The page shows the content of the file in Maple's folder.

34
00:02:29,936 --> 00:02:32,083
Cedar's prefix is garden.

35
00:02:32,083 --> 00:02:37,970
The same file name at /garden/robots.txt shows the content of Cedar's own file.

36
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:40,256
Each tenant serves its own.

37
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:52,316
The feature's startup registers an ITenantFileProvider, a physical file provider rooted at the tenant's wwwroot folder.

38
00:02:52,316 --> 00:02:57,346
It also registers it as an IStaticFileProvider, so other code can find it.

39
00:02:58,096 --> 00:03:02,397
In the tenant's pipeline, UseStaticFiles serves that provider.

40
00:03:02,397 --> 00:03:07,837
A file of an unknown type is sent as application/octet-stream, and each response

41
00:03:07,837 --> 00:03:10,936
carries a Cache-Control header for 30 days.

42
00:03:11,686 --> 00:03:16,574
In a view, a path that starts with ~/ includes the tenant's URL prefix.

43
00:03:16,574 --> 00:03:21,715
The asp-append-version attribute adds a version hash to the URL of a tenant

44
00:03:21,715 --> 00:03:27,746
file, because the file version provider also searches the tenant's static file providers.

45
00:03:31,946 --> 00:03:36,743
In the Orchard Core CMS web project, a file in the application's wwwroot

46
00:03:36,743 --> 00:03:41,170
folder is served before a tenant's file for the same request path.

47
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:45,783
If the SEO module is enabled, a robots.txt in the tenant folder takes

48
00:03:45,783 --> 00:03:48,796
precedence over the site's robots settings.

49
00:03:49,546 --> 00:03:53,587
Removing a tenant removes its site folder, wwwroot included.

50
00:03:53,587 --> 00:03:57,628
Keep your own copy of the files, to copy to the server again

51
00:03:57,628 --> 00:03:59,526
when you set up a tenant.

52
00:04:01,526 --> 00:04:05,686
Each tenant gets a wwwroot folder of its own, served at its own

53
00:04:05,686 --> 00:04:07,374
domain and URL prefix.

54
00:04:07,374 --> 00:04:10,208
That is the Static File Provider feature.

55
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:11,776
Thanks for watching.

